{"total_count":2,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2957","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2957/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2957/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2957/events","html_url":"https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2957","id":2763803468,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAzJbyc6GdyGG","number":2957,"title":"feat(completion): support sourcing zsh completion dynamically","user":{"login":"vegerot","id":5297725,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTc3MjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5297725?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot","html_url":"https://github.com/vegerot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vegerot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2024-12-30T23:36:56Z","updated_at":"2025-01-03T04:29:44Z","closed_at":"2024-12-31T13:23:13Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pulls/2957","html_url":"https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2957","diff_url":"https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2957.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2957.patch","merged_at":"2024-12-31T13:23:13Z"},"body":"Summary:\r\nPreviously, you needed to save the completion script to a file and then\r\nsource it.  Now, you can dynamically source completions in zsh by\r\nrunning\r\n\r\n```zsh\r\n$ source <(rg --generate complete-zsh)\r\n```\r\n\r\nTest plan:\r\n1. Run `source <(rg --generate complete-zsh)`\r\n2. Run `rg --generate=complete-zs<TAB>`\r\n\r\nBefore this commit, you would get an error after step 1.\r\nAfter this commit, it should work as expected.\r\n\r\nCloses #2956\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2957/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2957/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2684","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2684/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2684/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2684/events","html_url":"https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2684","id":2036215284,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAzJbyc5hthaD","number":2684,"title":"complete/fish: Make fish completion more intelligent","user":{"login":"blyxxyz","id":15526524,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NTI2NTI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15526524?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz","html_url":"https://github.com/blyxxyz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blyxxyz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2023-12-11T17:50:46Z","updated_at":"2024-01-08T15:54:35Z","closed_at":"2024-01-06T15:39:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pulls/2684","html_url":"https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2684","diff_url":"https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2684.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2684.patch","merged_at":"2024-01-06T15:39:35Z"},"body":"- Stop using `-n __fish_use_subcommand`. This had the effect of ignoring options if a positional argument has already been given, but that's not how ripgrep works.\r\n\r\n- Only suggest negation options if the option they're negating is passed (e.g., only complete `--no-pcre2` if `--pcre2` is present). The zsh completions already do this.\r\n\r\n- Take into account whether an option takes an argument. If an option is not a switch then it won't suggest further options until the argument is given, e.g. `-C<tab>` won't suggest options but `-i<tab>` will.\r\n\r\n- Suggest correct arguments for options. We already completed a fixed set of choices where available, but now we go further:\r\n\r\n  - Filenames are only suggested for options that take filenames.\r\n\r\n  - `--pre` and `--hostname-bin` suggest binaries from `$PATH`.\r\n\r\n  - `-t`/`--type`/&c use `--type-list` for suggestions, like in zsh, with a preview of the glob patterns:\r\n  ![image](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/assets/15526524/8b3f8a58-0177-48cd-9f20-67a039ef24f2)\r\n\r\n  - `--encoding` uses a hardcoded list extracted from the zsh completions. This has been refactored into a separate file, and the range globs (`{1..5}`) replaced by comma globs (`{1,2,3,4,5}`) since those work in both shells. I verified that this produces the same list as before in zsh, and the same list in fish (albeit in a different order).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2684/reactions","total_count":9,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":9,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/2684/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}